  "description": "Email Validator is an email validation API that checks whether an address is well-formed, whether its domain can receive mail, and whether it is safe to accept. It validates the format, resolves MX records (including null MX and the A-record fallback), checks for SPF and DMARC, flags disposable, role and free-provider addresses, and returns a normalized address for spotting duplicates. Paid plans add a risk score, typo correction, the mail provider and what a role mailbox is for (support, billing, noreply and so on).",
  "iconFile": "favicon@128.png",
